quantbot.lock
# The daemon's single-writer mutex. Its siblings above were ignored and this one was missed,
# so it was committed in 644752c. Runtime state does not belong in version control: git writes
# to it during a checkout while the daemon holds an exclusive OS lock on it, and every clone
# ships a stray file. It is not a liveness spoof -- `daemon_holds_lock` acquires the lock rather
# than checking the path -- but it has no business being tracked.
*.daemon.lock
crypto.db
crypto.lock
crypto-probe.db
crypto-probe.lock
research/stocks.db

# Local agent-tooling conveniences. `.codex-read-skills.cmd` was committed in 6bc3e4b (a
# catch-all "latest" commit), was referenced by nothing, and only ran `type` over three
# SKILL.md files under `C:\Users\JHutc\...` -- another machine's home directory, one of them
# pinned to a plugin cache version. It could not work for anyone else and had no project
# runtime purpose. Scratch files that describe one workstation do not belong in a repository
# two agents and two machines share.
.codex-read-skills.cmd
.codex/
.agents/
